HST Office: sw layout tests draw the fonts HST changes or previews with the fonts their documents were made with.

TestTdf150606 (CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter): the style gallery of the HST ribbon draws each style's name in the style's
own font, as the leading word processor does (hst-style-gallery.patch; upstream Writer has no such gallery in its
default user interface). After the test deletes its table, the gallery draws a style of tdf150606-1-min.odt that uses
Gentium Basic, which neither upstream nor HST bundles. On a user's system the font is substituted; in a CppunitTest the
test-only guard SAL_NON_APPLICATION_FONT_USE=abort aborted the whole suite there and hid every later test. The test
maps Gentium Basic to the bundled Liberation Serif for its duration; the document's text does not use the font (its
layout would hit the same guard), so the layout it checks is unchanged.

testTdf108021, testTdf125334, testTdf127304 (CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter2): a chart without fonts of its own takes the
default spreadsheet font, Calibri in HST (hst-msoffice-defaults.patch), drawn with the narrower bundled Carlito, so its
axis labels need fewer lines and no rotation (4 instead of 8 and 0 instead of 4 wrapped labels, no 90 degree labels).
These tests check the label wrapping and rotation of documents made with upstream's Liberation Sans, so they draw
Calibri with Liberation Sans for their duration.

Both substitutions are removed, and the font caches cleared, when the test ends.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: make CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter CppunitTest_sw_layoutwriter2.
